WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.860
These two cute koalas
are a background image inside a div.

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:07.740
And right now,
the background size it set to cover.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:11.306
I want you to compare the difference
between background size cover and

00:00:11.306 --> 00:00:12.705
background size contain.

00:00:12.705 --> 00:00:14.918
It might help if you
resize the page a bit,

00:00:14.918 --> 00:00:17.392
to figure out the difference
between the two.

00:00:17.392 --> 00:00:20.304
Once you think you know the difference
between cover and contain,

00:00:20.304 --> 00:00:21.930
I have two statements for you.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:24.150
The first one says that
the image is sized so

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:29.100
that it is as small as possible while
still completely filling its container.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.370
Is that describing contain or cover?

00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:31.970
Pick one of the two.

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:36.140
And the second statement says, the image
is sized so that it is as large as

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:40.170
possible while still being completely
visible inside its container.

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:42.730
Is this statement describing contain or
cover?

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:43.580
Pick one of these two.

